(;FF[4]CA[UTF-8]GM[1]SZ[19]GN[Created by 5-dan player Yin Hang. Commentary: I think the practicality of life-and-death problems is very important. Life-and-death problems without practical reference value always seem to deviate from the original intention of my creation. In addition, the number of stones in the shape of the problem should be minimized to make the problem look more aesthetically pleasing. This was told to me by Cui Can when he helped me simplify a certain problem. Since then, I've also started to pay attention to the problem of simplifying useless stones.]GC[Type: Life & Death | Level: 6D | Rating: 4.8/5 | Correct: 31% (292/929) | Desc: Created by 5-dan player Yin Hang. Commentary: I think the practicality of life-and-death problems is very important. Life-and-death problems without practical reference value always seem to deviate from the original intention of my creation. In addition, the number of stones in the shape of the problem should be minimized to make the problem look more aesthetically pleasing. This was told to me by Cui Can when he helped me simplify a certain problem. Since then, I've also started to pay attention to the problem of simplifying useless stones. | First move: Black]AB[pb]AB[qd]AB[qh]AW[nb]AW[nc]AW[nd]AW[od]AW[of]AW[qf]AW[rf]AW[qg](;B[sb](;W[ra](;B[re](;W[pa];B[oa];W[ob];B[qa];W[qb](;B[rb];W[pa]C[RIGHT])(;B[qc];W[pa]C[RIGHT])(;B[pc];W[pa]C[RIGHT]))(;W[pc](;B[qc];W[pa];B[oa];W[qb];B[qa]C[RIGHT])(;B[qb];W[se];B[sd];W[rc];B[qc];W[rb];B[sf];W[sg];B[ob];W[rd];B[qe];W[se]C[RIGHT]))(;W[rc];B[rb];W[qc];B[pc];W[rd];B[qe](;W[se];B[sd]C[RIGHT])(;W[qb];B[sd];W[pa];B[oa];W[ob];B[qa]C[RIGHT])))(;B[rb];W[pc];B[qc];W[qa];B[pa];W[sd]C[WRONG]))(;W[rc];B[rd];W[rb];B[ra];W[sc];B[sd];W[sa];B[qb];W[pa];B[qc];W[qa];B[oa];W[ob];B[ra];W[qa];B[pa]C[RIGHT])(;W[sd];B[se](;W[re];B[ra];W[rc];B[rd];W[qc];B[pc];W[sf];B[qb];W[pd];B[oa]C[RIGHT])(;W[pc](;B[qc];W[ra];B[re];W[pa];B[oa];W[qb];B[qa]C[RIGHT])(;B[qb];W[re];B[ra];W[rc]C[WRONG])))(;W[pa];B[oa];W[ob